# Front-End 4.83/5 #
- **Layout and visual presentation**  4/5
    - The design is neat, simple and fits the theme about the owner's project relating to cars and travel. The entire thing doesn't look off, the colours chosen for this website doesn't clash with each other too. It's simple, direct at telling you where is where, harmonises with each other without clashing. The thing preventing me from giving a 5 start is how the Login page isn't centered. Though that was the intent of the owner, it just seemed off and the car at the other side doesn't seem to give enough weight to make the page look balanced.
- **Usability and navigation** 5/5
    - The navigation is very easy and direct. The website tells you where to go with the directions in the navigation bar. It's very usable too, barely any errors when booted up and most of the buttons can be used to redirect or do something when pressed. If improved, it might be a good website for joining community riding.
- **Consistency**  5/5
    - Visually consistent with the theme of cars and the use of the greyscale with red as the only non-grey in it. The elements in the web design are also very proportionate with each other, each size being consistent towards others. In terms of code, it uses a css which made it easier to use a consistent design within a feature.
- **Readability**  5/5
    - The readability in the design is good visually. In terms of code, it was easy to tell which one is inside each features. The naming conventions in the css is also very much easy to follow on which one is being used in the design.
- **Responsiveness, if applicable**  5/5
    - The responsiveness of the website is very high. The buttons work and the barely causes errors when clicking something. The map is also very much interactive which adds to the responsiveness of the website, being able to zoom in and out using the buttons and touching the locations in screen.
- **Overall completeness and functionality** 5/5
    - Despite it being very simple, the design is on point to the theme of the website. It's very easy to navigate, use, and the website is easy to respond when it is being used. The design and the code is consistent and true to its name so it's a really good website. Simple but pleasing.
**Average: 5 + 3 + 5 + 4 + 5 + 4.5 = 26.5/6 = 4.83**
